    "diff_hunk": "@@ -114318,6 +114327,35 @@ new PaymentRequest(&hellip;); // Allowed to use\n      <span>map of active timers</span>.</p></li>\n     </ol>\n    </li>\n+\n+   <li>\n+    <p>Otherwise, for each <code>EventSource</code> object <var>eventSource</var> whose\n+    <span>relevant global object</span> is equal to <var>window</var>, if\n+    <var>eventSource</var>'s <code data-x=\"dom-EventSource-readyState\">readyState</code>\n+    attribute is not <code data-x=\"dom-EventSource-CLOSED\">CLOSED</code> and there are any\n+    ongoing instances of the <span data-x=\"concept-fetch\">fetch</span> algorithm started for\n+    <var>eventSource</var>, then:</p>\n+\n+    <ol>\n+     <li><p>Abort those instances of the <span data-x=\"concept-fetch\">fetch</span> algorithm.\n+     Their <i data-x=\"processResponse\">processResponse</i> and <i\n+     data-x=\"processResponseEndOfBody\">processResponseEndOfBody</i> steps must do nothing if\n+     subsequently invoked. Discard any pending tasks queued by the <span>announce the\n+     connection</span> algorithm for those instances, and any further data received from the\n+     network for them.</p></li>\n+\n+     <li><p>Set <var>eventSource</var>'s <code\n+     data-x=\"dom-EventSource-readyState\">readyState</code> attribute to <code\n+     data-x=\"dom-EventSource-CONNECTING\">CONNECTING</code>.</p></li>\n+\n+     <li><p>Set <var>eventSource</var>'s <span\n+     data-x=\"concept-event-stream-reconnect-after-bfcache\">reconnect after back/forward cache\n+     restoration</span> flag to true.</p></li>\n+    </ol>\n+\n+    <p class=\"note\">Tasks that were already <span data-x=\"queue a task\">queued</span> to dispatch",
