    "body": " Updated to fire `error` on BFCache restoration, then reconnect unless the `error` handler closes the EventSource. Reconnection fires `open` on success or `error` on failure.\r\n\r\nThis skips the reconnection delay (including `retry:`), since the interruption is caused by BFCache rather than a network or server failure. Does that sound OK?",
